/dataset-rgb
/dataset-dutch-rgb
/.history

# Technical reliability screening: large regenerable image output (crops, normalized-page blobs,
# export-package PNGs) derived from dataset-rgb/ -- reproducible from committed hashes/config, not
# committed itself. The small evidence records (telemetry JSONL, results JSON, PAGE XML, manifests)
# ARE committed -- only the binary image bytes are excluded here.
docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/**/blobs/
docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/**/crops/
docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/**/export-packages/**/*.png

# Lion-vs-Loghi launcher output (scripts/run_lion_loghi_comparison.py): telemetry/reports from local
# runs, not committed evidence -- committed evidence for this comparison lives in this same directory
# tree but outside runs/, added deliberately per file (dataset-comparability.md, README.md, ...).
docs/experiments/lion-loghi-comparison/runs/

# Loghi upstream (git clone of knaw-huc/loghi + submodules, plus downloaded pretrained checkpoints)
# -- large, locally-assembled, never committed, same discipline as .venv-satrn/ above.
.loghi-upstream/

# Swedish Loghi fine-tuning (pilot + full-corpus runs, docs/methods/loghi-swedish-finetuning.md and
# loghi-full-corpus-training.md): real Keras checkpoints, extracted line-image PNGs, and the full
# source inventory are large and regenerable from the real dataset + committed manifests/config --
# not committed, same "small evidence committed, large regenerable blobs excluded" discipline as
# docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/ above. Manifests, reports, and derived monitoring
# config (small, real evidence -- split composition, character-compatibility/memory-probe/resume-proof
# results, pilot-derived monitoring values) ARE committed.
# `run-state/` is excluded by its heavy subpaths rather than wholesale, so the small JSON evidence
# beside them stays under version control. `run_state.json` is the run's audit file by design and
# `session_state.json` carries the real validation history -- excluding the whole directory meant a
# completed training run left no committed record of what it actually did. Measured on the 53-shard
# full-corpus run: epoch_output 39.5GB, staged_parent_checkpoint 497MB, telemetry 1.5MB and growing,
# versus 225KB for everything kept. `integrity_cache.json` is excluded too -- it is a regenerable
# cache keyed on file mtimes, so committing it would churn on every run without adding evidence.
# Every pattern here is depth-independent (`**`). Single-level equivalents were tried first and
# missed 3.98GB sitting in nested paths the flat form does not reach -- run-state/resume-proof/
# epoch_output/, run-state/memory-probe/, run-state/smoke-staged-parent/ -- the same shape of miss
# that previously let 141MB of shard Parquet reach the remote.
training/**/epoch_output/
training/**/staged_parent_checkpoint/
training/**/smoke-staged-parent/
# Disposable copies the lap evaluation mounts read-write so inference cannot mutate the recorded
# checkpoint. Regenerated on demand; the evaluation's real evidence is results.txt and
# lap_evaluation.json beside them.
training/**/staged_checkpoint/
training/**/memory-probe/
training/**/inspect_out/
training/**/telemetry/
training/**/integrity_cache.json
# Backstop independent of directory naming: serialized model weights are the actual weight, and a
# future run directory that invents a new subdirectory name must not be able to smuggle them in.
training/**/*.keras
training/**/*.keras.old
training/**/*.h5
training/**/*.hdf5
training/**/*.pb
training/*/prepared-data/
training/*/source-inventory/
training/*/shards/
# Also match nested run directories (e.g. training/_superseded_prepared_runs/<run>/shards/),
# which the single-level pattern above misses -- 141MB of regenerable shard Parquet reached
# the remote before this was noticed.
training/**/shards/

# Shared full-corpus training-data pool: ~562k extracted line-image PNGs (~85GB) plus the
# per-shard training lists, all regenerable from the source dataset + committed manifests by
# `full_run prepare`. Same "small evidence committed, large regenerable blobs excluded"
# discipline as the run directories above. Also keeps `git status` fast -- with these files
# untracked-but-scanned it took ~44s, which silently blew the launch manifest's dirty-check
# timeout and made it record a clean tree that was not clean.
training/_prepared_data/

# Disposable preflight smoke-test output: real container checkpoints (~1.6GB per run),
# regenerated by every `preflight` invocation and never evidence of anything.
training/preflight-check/

# Editable-install build metadata (regenerated by `pip install -e .` every time; not source).
*.egg-info/

# Superseded prepared runs: kept on disk as audit evidence, but their contents are regenerable
# and already described in docs/audits/. Not tracked.
training/_superseded_prepared_runs/

# Independent Loghi-vs-Lion benchmark data (docs/BENCHMARK_PROTOCOL.md): incoming deliveries,
# derived work, frozen benchmarks and prediction reports. Contains third-party archive images and
# GT; frozen manifests are identified by SHA-256 recorded in each report, not by git.
benchmark-data/
